---
// The private posting studio. Not linked from the site, noindex, robots disallow, locked behind Cloudflare Access.
import '../../src/styles/global.css';
import { sharePosts } from '../../src/lib/share';
import { summary, lastSuccessDate } from '../../src/lib/data';
import { longDate } from '../../src/lib/format';
import { plan } from '../lib/plan';
import { PITCHES, draft } from '../lib/pitch';

const today = new Date();
const slots = plan(new Date(Date.UTC(today.getUTCFullYear(), today.getUTCMonth(), today.getUTCDate())), 14);
const kinds = [...new Set(sharePosts.map((p) => p.kind))];
const mail = draft();
const thisMonth = today.toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { month: 'long', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' });
const due = PITCHES.find((p) => p.month === thisMonth) ?? PITCHES[0];
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-GB">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
  <title>Studio | Galamsey Tracker</title>
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
  <script is:inline>
    try { const t = localStorage.getItem('theme'); if (t) document.documentElement.dataset.theme = t; } catch {}
  </script>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="top">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="brand">Galamsey Tracker studio</p>
      <button class="icon theme" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-label="Switch to dark mode">
        <svg class="moon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 14.5A8.5 8.5 0 0 1 9.5 4a8.5 8.5 0 1 0 10.5 10.5Z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        <svg class="sun" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M12 2v2.5M12 19.5V22M2 12h2.5M19.5 12H22M4.9 4.9l1.8 1.8M17.3 17.3l1.8 1.8M4.9 19.1l1.8-1.8M17.3 6.7l1.8-1.8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
      </button>
      <nav aria-label="Studio"><a href="#next">Next posts</a><a href="#posts">All posts</a><a href="#pitch">Pitch emails</a><a href="#how">How we post</a></nav>
    </div>
  </header>
  <main class="wrap">
    <p class="lede">{summary && <>Made from the satellite data up to {longDate(summary.data_date)}. </>}{lastSuccessDate && <>Last weekly update: {longDate(lastSuccessDate)}. </>}This page is not linked or listed anywhere. Keep the address to yourself.</p>

    <section id="next">
      <h1>Next posts</h1>
      <p>Post from @GalamseyTracker at about 19:00 GMT. On the best post of the week, quote it from your own account with one line in your own words. If galamsey news breaks about a place we cover, ask Claude for a "One place" post instead.</p>
      <ol class="slots">
        {slots.map((s) => (
          <li>
            <span class="day">{s.day}</span>
            <a href={`#${s.slug}`}>{s.title}</a>
            {s.pitch && <a class="pitch" href="#pitch">Also today: send this month's pitch email (how, below)</a>}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="posts">
      <h2>All posts this week</h2>
      <p>Every kind of post, made fresh from this week's data. Kinds: {kinds.join(', ')}.</p>
      <div class="posts">
        {sharePosts.map((p) => (
          <article id={p.slug} class="post">
            {!p.title.startsWith(p.kind) && <p class="kind">{p.kind}</p>}
            <h3>{p.title}</h3>
            <a href={`/${p.slug}.jpg`}><img src={`/${p.slug}.jpg`} alt={p.alt} width="1080" height="1350" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a>
            <p><a class="btn" href={`/${p.slug}.jpg`} download={`galamsey-${p.slug}.jpg`}>Save the image</a></p>
            {[['Post', p.text], ['Image description (alt text)', p.alt], ['First reply, with the link', p.reply]].map(([label, value]) => (
              <div class="copy">
                <div class="head"><h4>{label}</h4><button type="button" class="btn" data-copy>Copy</button></div>
                <p data-text>{value}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="pitch" class="how">
      <h2>Pitch emails</h2>
      <h3>What this is</h3>
      <p>Once a month you send one short email to one journalist or organisation, offering them the data for a story. A single news story or report that uses the data reaches far more people than our own posts, and the people who read it are the ones who act. You send it from hello@galamseytracker.org, so it comes from the project, not your personal address.</p>
      <h3>This month: {due.month}</h3>
      <dl class="due">
        <dt>To</dt><dd>{due.who}</dd>
        <dt>Address</dt><dd>{due.verified ? <><a href={`mailto:${due.contact}`}>{due.contact}</a> (from their own contact page)</> : due.contact}</dd>
        <dt>Angle</dt><dd>{due.angle}</dd>
      </dl>
      {mail && due === PITCHES[0] && (
        <>
          <div class="copy"><div class="head"><h4>Subject</h4><button type="button" class="btn" data-copy>Copy</button></div><p data-text>{mail.subject}</p></div>
          <div class="copy"><div class="head"><h4>Email</h4><button type="button" class="btn" data-copy>Copy</button></div><p data-text>{mail.body}</p></div>
        </>
      )}
      {due !== PITCHES[0] && <p>Ask Claude in the project: "draft this month's pitch email". It finds the right reporter's address, writes the email from this week's numbers and saves it for you.</p>}
      <h3>How to send it (Gmail on your phone or computer)</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>Open Gmail and start a new email.</li>
        <li>Tap the From line and choose hello@galamseytracker.org. You set this up as "Send mail as" in October.</li>
        <li>Put the address above in To. Send to one person or newsroom at a time, never a list.</li>
        <li>Copy the subject and the email from this page and paste them in. Read it once, change anything that does not sound like you.</li>
        <li>Send it on a weekday morning, Tuesday to Thursday, when newsrooms plan their stories.</li>
        <li>If there is no reply after a week, send one short follow-up in the same thread ("Just checking this reached you. Happy to pull numbers for any district or river."). Then leave it.</li>
        <li>If they reply, answer within a day, and ask Claude to pull whatever they ask for.</li>
      </ol>
      <h3>Who comes next</h3>
      <ol class="queue">
        {PITCHES.map((p) => <li><strong>{p.month}:</strong> {p.who}. {p.angle}</li>)}
      </ol>
      <h3>What not to do</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>No attachments. Links only, so it does not land in spam.</li>
        <li>No claims the site does not make: never call a place illegal or name anyone.</li>
        <li>No mass emails or newsletters. One person, one angle, one month.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="how" class="how">
      <h2>How we post</h2>
      <h3>The goal</h3>
      <p>Not retweets. The goal is that the satellite evidence keeps reaching the people who can act on it: city readers who drink the water, the diaspora, journalists, NGOs and cocoa buyers. We watch visits from X, WhatsApp and Facebook in Cloudflare Web Analytics, emails to hello@, and journalists or NGOs using the data.</p>
      <h3>Two accounts</h3>
      <p>@GalamseyTracker posts the evidence three times a week, by hand from your phone. Never scripted: X bans that. Your own account quote-posts the best one each week with one line in your own words, so your followers see it and your feed stays yours.</p>
      <h3>Every post</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>One picture that stands alone, one true fact, a plain last line.</li>
        <li>No questions to readers. People quote with their own take.</li>
        <li>The link goes in the account's own first reply, to the page about that place or city.</li>
        <li>Add the image description when you post. It helps people using screen readers, and X shows it to everyone who taps "ALT".</li>
        <li>No accusations, no names. "Likely galamsey" is our guess.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Beyond X</h3>
      <p>Send the same image to your WhatsApp Status and family groups, and to Facebook hometown and diaspora groups. Once each: Reddit r/ghana and r/dataisbeautiful, Hacker News "Show HN", LinkedIn.</p>
      <h3>Once a month</h3>
      <p>A short email from hello@ to one journalist or NGO, with one ready angle. Before 30 December lead with cocoa and the EU deforestation law, which starts that day. Ask Claude for the draft.</p>
      <h3>New kinds of post</h3>
      <p>On a posting day, Claude can design a new kind of post when one is due, through the same plan, critique and redo as these. Ideas waiting: forest reserves, cocoa districts, a month in review, a place's picture every few months.</p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script is:inline>
    const root = document.documentElement;
    const dark = () => root.dataset.theme ? root.dataset.theme === 'dark' : matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches;
    const label = () => document.querySelectorAll('[data-theme-toggle]').forEach((b) => b.setAttribute('aria-label', dark() ? 'Switch to light mode' : 'Switch to dark mode'));
    label();
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-theme-toggle]').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
      root.dataset.theme = dark() ? 'light' : 'dark';
      try { localStorage.setItem('theme', root.dataset.theme); } catch {}
      label();
    }));
  </script>
  <script>
    for (const b of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy]')) {
      b.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        const text = b.closest('.copy')!.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-text]')!.innerText;
        try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text); b.textContent = 'Copied'; } catch { b.textContent = 'Select and copy'; }
        setTimeout(() => (b.textContent = 'Copy'), 2000);
      });
    }
  </script>

  <style>
    body { background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); }
    .top { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .top .wrap { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 24px; padding-top: 14px; padding-bottom: 14px; }
    .brand { margin: 0; font-weight: 800; flex: 1; }
    .icon { font: inherit; color: var(--ink); background: transparent; cursor: pointer; display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
            justify-content: center; min-width: 44px; min-height: 44px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 0; }
    .icon:hover { border-color: var(--ink); }
    .theme .sun { display: none; }
    :root[data-theme='dark'] .theme .sun { display: block; }
    :root[data-theme='dark'] .theme .moon { display: none; }
    @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
      :root:not([data-theme='light']) .theme .sun { display: block; }
      :root:not([data-theme='light']) .theme .moon { display: none; }
    }
    nav { width: 100%; }
    .due { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 6px 16px; margin: 0 0 8px; }
    .due dt { font-weight: 700; }
    .due dd { margin: 0; }
    .queue li, .how ol li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
    nav { display: flex; gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    nav a { color: var(--ink); }
    .lede { color: var(--muted); margin: 24px 0; }
    h1 { margin: 0 0 8px; }
    section { margin-bottom: 56px; max-width: 70ch; }
    #posts { max-width: none; }
    .slots { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 16px 0 0; display: grid; gap: 10px; }
    .slots li { display: grid; gap: 4px; padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .day { font-weight: 700; }
    .pitch { color: var(--signal); font-weight: 700; }
    .posts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(320px, 1fr)); gap: 48px 32px; margin-top: 24px; }
    .kind { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9375rem; }
    .post h3 { margin: 2px 0 12px; }
    .post img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .copy { margin-top: 14px; }
    .head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 12px; }
    h4 { margin: 0; font-size: 1rem; }
    [data-text] { white-space: pre-line; margin: 6px 0 0; padding: 12px; border: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: 0.9375rem; }
    .how li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  </style>
</body>
</html>
